title: Links in the Scene view
intro: Select something and the Scene view shows what it's linked to: arrows to the entities its fields name, and from the ones that name it.
project: Platformer | Links

chapter: What a lever works | Arrows to what it names
select: Lever
look: -8, 0, 6
expectlink: Lever > Bridge = Switch Targets
explain: link:Lever > Bridge | Switch Targets | The lever brings out the bridge. Its Targets name it, so an arrow runs from the lever to the bridge, labelled with the field.
expectlink: Lever > Hint = Switch Prompt
say: Its Prompt gets one too: the little hint above it, its own child.
pickentity: Switch.Targets = Lift
expectlink: Lever > Lift = Switch Targets
explain: link:Lever > Lift | A new target | Name the lift as well, and a second arrow appears. No more reading names in the Inspector and hunting for them in the level.

chapter: What names it | Arrows the other way
select: Player
look: -3, 1, 6
expectlink: Main Camera > Player = Follow Target
expectlink: Player > Health Bar = Health
explain: link:Main Camera > Player | Follow Target | Nothing on the player names the camera, but the camera's Follow names the player, so selecting the player shows that arrow too, pointing at it.
explain: link:Player > Health Bar | Health | And the health bar reads the player's health, so that arrow comes from the player, labelled with what it reads. Before deleting or renaming something, you can see everything that depends on it.
select: Lever
pickentity: Switch.Targets = Lift
expectlink: Lever > Lift = none
say: Take the lift out of the lever's targets, and its arrow goes with it.
